+`init`, `status`, `check`, `apply`, `use`, `link`, `unlink`, `bucket`, `map`, and `scope` (and each of their subcommands) accept `--help` (`-h`), which prints command-specific usage and exits 0 without needing an initialized project. Unexpected positional arguments, flags that do not belong to the subcommand, and conflicting selectors (`--all` with `--scope`, both `--before` and `--after`) are usage errors (exit 3).
 
